# Read-only observations

Workspace aae7db361c7f: request 11946 submitted 2026-10-20T19:41:46-05:00,
replied 19:42:26. Request 11947 queued 19:52:53 while native compact attempts
failed with an upstream model-alias HTTP 400. After the 19:55 launch, the
poller repeatedly logs pre_submit wake_history_incomplete at physical line
12888 and delivery_held. Later peer report lists request 11983 still queued;
that later report is supplied evidence, not an independently rerun measurement.

The read-only status-file scan found two non-JSON physical lines:
12888 has 119 NUL bytes before a surviving replied record for 4606;
30025 has 314 NUL bytes before a surviving queued record for 10342.
Neither proves why bytes are NUL or that no ownership record was overwritten.
Do not treat prefix removal as proof that history is complete.

# Attribution correction

The first queued input predates the update observation. The current strict
history hold explains later non-submission, not the entire original outage.
The 1b08402 change keeps the CLI alive while withholding delivery when strict
ownership parsing fails. Earlier f6fc7ac also had strict reconciliation code.
No claim that an update created the NULs is supported.

# Boundaries and authorized work

User requested source improvements, local deployment and nightly push.
No live history repair, queue replay, cursor reset, quarantine activation or
session restart is authorized by that source-deployment request.

Implement payload-free history diagnostics and read-only queue-age/blocker
visibility separately from queued/submitted/replied. Keep event-ack/1 queued
receipt separate from actual injected receipt. Any future recovery boundary
must explicitly quarantine all pre-boundary uncertainty rather than replay it,
and requires a stale-safe preview and separate confirmation.

# Verification status

Implementation and owned acceptance are in progress. This document does not
claim a restored Walkie backlog or deployed fix.

# Follow-up authorization

User explicitly requested that after local and nightly deployment, this session
contact ciel-walkie over the Claude socket, ask that session to restart through
its Ciel Runtime MCP, and coordinate until actual SSE-to-session delivery works.
This authorizes that later restart coordination, not arbitrary history repair,
queue replay, cursor resets or fabricated injection receipts. Verify newly
received input transitions queued -> submitted -> replied, not only SSE receipt.
